From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thecorporatetractor <marco@azarguard.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:20:25 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 10/15] core: add series_stats, series_fit_line,
 series_outliers, series_decompose(_anomalies)

New functions on dynamic-array series (make-series output):
- series_stats (tuple: min, min_idx, max, max_idx, avg, variance, stdev) and
  series_stats_dynamic (the same as a bag); variance is the sample variance.
- series_fit_line (tuple: rsquare, slope, variance, rvariance, interception,
  line_fit) and series_fit_line_dynamic; least squares over x = 0..n-1.
- series_outliers(series [, kind, ignore_val, min_percentile, max_percentile]):
  Tukey-fence score per point ('ctukey' p10/p90 by default, 'tukey' p25/p75).
- series_decompose(series [, seasonality, trend, test_points]) -> (baseline,
  seasonal, trend, residual), trend 'avg' | 'linefit' | 'none'.
- series_decompose_anomalies(series [, threshold, seasonality, trend,
  test_points, method]) -> (ad_flag, ad_score, baseline): the residual of the
  decomposition scored with series_outliers; |score| > threshold (default 1.5)
  flags +1/-1.

Tuple results: Kusto types these calls as tuples (extend (a, b) = f(s), or
bare extend f(s) with generated column names). A tuple call now translates to
an IRTupleScalarCallNode holding one scalar call per tuple column, which
extend, project and print expand into columns. The functions are evaluated row
by row from raw argument values (RowwiseScalarFunctionImpl).

Approximations: seasonality = -1 detects the period from the autocorrelation
of the detrended series (shortest local maximum within 90 % of the best lag,
accepted above 0.3), not ADX's periodogram; the seasonal component is the
per-phase median. Clear anomalies get the same flags as ADX; scores and
baselines are close, not identical. series_stats ignores non-finite values
whatever ignore_nonfinite says. seasonality_threshold is not supported.
